-- ── ADDITIONAL REHAB COST ITEMS ──────────────────────────────
('Attic/Insulation','Attic Insulation Upgrade to R-38','replacement','per_home',1500,3000,5000,'Florida attics reach 150°F+ in summer. Proper insulation critical for HVAC efficiency and buyer appeal. Blown-in insulation typical. Must have proper soffit ventilation.','Damaged batt insulation from prior work','5','Thin or no insulation visible from attic hatch, high utility bills reported by sellers','Insulation directly affects HVAC runtime and buyer utility costs. Good marketing point for energy efficiency.'),
('Attic/Insulation','Air Sealing Package','repair','per_home',800,1800,3500,'Seal all penetrations: light fixtures, HVAC boots, plumbing penetrations. Often overlooked but significant energy impact.','Labor intensive to do properly','10','Drafts, high utility bills, comfort complaints','Pair with insulation upgrade for maximum benefit.'),
('Garage','Garage Door Replacement','replacement','each',1200,1900,3500,'Steel single: $1,200-1,800. Steel double: $1,800-2,800. Insulated double: $2,200-3,500. Impact-rated adds 20-30%.','Track replacement if damaged','5','Dented, off-track, non-functional, manual only','Garage door is high-visibility. Counts in curb appeal immediately.'),
('Garage','Garage Door Opener','replacement','each',350,500,900,'Belt drive preferred for quiet operation. Include keypad and remotes. Smart/wifi opener adds $100-200.','Wiring issues in older homes','5','No opener, broken spring (replace door and opener together)','Budget $500 per garage opener installed. Always include on flips.'),
('Garage','Garage Floor Coating','full','per_home',1500,2800,5000,'Epoxy coating for garage floor. Transforms appearance. Popular with buyers. 1-2 day install.','Floor cracks, moisture issues','10','Oil stains, cracked bare concrete','High ROI for the cost. $2,500 epoxy floor dramatically upgrades garage perception.'),
('Exterior','Stucco Repair and Paint','repair','per_home',2000,5000,12000,'Florida stucco is common on CBS homes. Cracks allow water intrusion — must seal. Elastomeric paint required over stucco. Full repaint over stucco: $4,000-8,000 per home.','Hidden water damage behind stucco cracks','25','Stucco cracks, efflorescence (white staining), delamination, soft spots when pressed','Never skip stucco cracks. Water intrusion creates mold and structural damage quickly in Florida humidity.'),
('Exterior','Pressure Washing','repair','per_home',250,500,1000,'Driveway, walkway, pool deck, exterior walls, screens. Often transforms curb appeal dramatically. Should be done before listing always.','None significant','0','Algae/mold growth on surfaces, dirty driveway/walkways','Always include pressure wash. Cost is minimal, impact is substantial.'),
('Exterior','Soffit and Fascia Repair','repair','per_home',800,2500,8000,'Common failure point in Florida from moisture and pests. Wood soffit/fascia rots. Vinyl or aluminum replacement preferred. Often needed when reroofing.','Rotted wood extent often larger than visible','30','Peeling paint, soft spots, holes, bird/insect damage','Always inspect soffit/fascia closely on any roof job. Often overlooked until bird nests appear.'),
('Exterior','Gutters and Downspouts','replacement','per_home',1200,2000,4000,'Seamless aluminum gutters with downspouts. 6" K-style preferred for Florida rainfall. Gutter guards add $1,000-2,500.','Underground drainage issues at downspout exit','5','Pulling away from fascia, pooling water near foundation','Florida rainfall is intense. Proper guttering protects foundation. Include on any flip.'),
('Exterior','Fence Installation','full','per_home',3000,5500,12000,'Wood privacy (6ft): $25-35/lf installed. Vinyl privacy: $30-45/lf. Aluminum: $25-40/lf. Chain link: $15-25/lf. Corner lots need more fencing.','Property line disputes during install','10','No fence on corner lot where buyers expect it, damaged existing fence','Privacy fence adds value on right properties. Check if neighborhood has fence restrictions.'),
('Exterior','Fence Repair','repair','per_home',500,1500,4000,'Repair or replace sections. Post replacement $150-300/post. Panel replacement $40-80/panel.','Extensive root damage requiring full replacement','20','Leaning posts, rotted wood, broken panels, gates not functioning','Budget $1,000 fence repairs on any property with existing fence.'),
('Exterior','Driveway Resurfacing','repair','per_home',1500,3000,6000,'Asphalt seal coat: $500-1,000. Asphalt overlay: $2,000-4,000. Concrete: $4,000-8,000. Pavers: $8,000-15,000.','Extensive cracking requiring full removal','15','Major cracking, heaving, large holes, severe discoloration','Cracked driveway kills curb appeal. Sealcoat minimum; replace if structural failure.'),
('Pool','Pool Resurfacing','full','per_home',4500,8000,14000,'Plaster: $4,500-7,000. Quartz (PebbleTec): $8,000-12,000. Tile: $12,000-16,000. Florida pools resurface every 10-15 years.','Structural cracks during gunite','20','Rough surfaces, calcium deposits, staining, plaster failure','Pool resurfacing dramatically improves appearance and function. Budget for it on older pools.'),
('Pool','Pool Equipment Replacement','replacement','per_home',2000,4500,9000,'Pump: $800-1,500. Filter: $500-1,000. Heater: $2,000-4,000. Salt system: $1,200-2,000. Variable speed pump: $1,200-2,000.','Underground plumbing leaks','20','Non-functioning equipment, single-speed pump (inefficient), missing heater','Variable speed pump required by code in FL. If replacing any equipment, assess all at same time.'),
('Pool','Screen Enclosure Repair','repair','per_home',800,2500,8000,'Screen replacement: $0.60-1.00/sqft. Structural repair: $100-300/panel. Full rescreening typical: $2,000-5,000.','Structural frame damage requiring replacement','15','Holes, tears, green algae on screens, bowed frames','Budget screen repair on any pool home. Buyers notice immediately.'),
('Pool','Pool Safety Fence','replacement','per_home',1200,2000,4000,'Required by FL law when pool present and child under 6 in household. Code requires pool barrier when selling.','None significant','5','No pool barrier on older homes','FL law 515.27: pool must have barrier. Required disclosure item. Install before listing.'),
('Security','Security System Rough-In','replacement','per_home',500,1200,2500,'Pre-wire for cameras, door/window sensors, panel location. Buyers install their own system on smart home prep.','None significant','5','No security rough-in','Smart home prep is low cost, high perceived value. Add to any $350K+ flip.'),
('SmartHome','Smart Home Package','replacement','per_home',800,1800,3500,'Nest/Ecobee thermostat ($250), smart locks ($200-400/door), video doorbell ($200-400), basic smart lighting. Appeals to tech-savvy buyers.','None significant','5','No smart home features','Budget $1,500 smart home package on $350K+ flips. High perceived value relative to cost.'),
('Water','Water Softener System','replacement','per_home',800,1500,3000,'Florida hard water is very common, especially Pasco and Hillsborough. Causes appliance damage, spots on fixtures. Buyers increasingly expect this in certain areas.','Softener brine tank placement, drainage requirements','5','Hard water staining on fixtures, scale on appliances','Consider on Pasco/east Hillsborough flips where water is hardest. Buyers from Northeast expect soft water.'),
('Water','Water Treatment/Filtration','replacement','per_home',400,900,2500,'Reverse osmosis under sink: $400-800. Whole house filter: $500-1,500. Important in areas with well water or water quality concerns.','None significant','5','Yellow/brown water, strong chlorine smell, sulfur (rotten egg) smell','In Spring Hill/Hernando with well water: include water treatment in scope always.'),
('HVAC','UV Air Purifier (In-Duct)','replacement','per_home',400,700,1200,'UV light kills mold and bacteria in HVAC. Post-COVID buyers increasingly want air quality features. Easy install in air handler.','None significant','5','Musty smell from vents, mold history in home','Low cost, high marketing value. Include in $350K+ flip scope.'),
('Electrical','EV Charging Prep (240V Outlet)','replacement','per_home',800,1400,2500,'Install 240V/50A outlet in garage for EV charging. Increasingly expected by buyers. Especially in Wesley Chapel/New Tampa.','Panel capacity must support','10','No 240V garage outlet','Budget $1,200 EV prep on any 2024+ flip. Buyer expectation shifting quickly.'),
('Electrical','LED Lighting Package','replacement','per_home',600,1200,2500,'All LED fixtures throughout. Recessed lighting in kitchen, living. Ceiling fans in bedrooms. Modern light bars in baths. Buyers notice immediately.','Dimmers incompatible with some LEDs','5','Fluorescent kitchen lights, outdated ceiling fans, brass/bronze fixtures','Modern lighting completely transforms interior perception. Always include.'),
('Kitchen','Kitchen Cabinet Painting','repair','per_home',2500,4500,8000,'Paint and refinish existing cabinet boxes and replace doors/hardware. Cost-effective alternative to full replacement when boxes are solid. Popular technique for budget flips.','Cabinet boxes must be structurally sound','15','Cabinet boxes damaged, particle board swelling, soft spots in boxes','Cabinet painting works when boxes are solid. Inspect carefully before committing.'),
('Kitchen','Quartz Countertop Install','replacement','per_home',3000,5500,9000,'Quartz (engineered stone) is the current buyer expectation for $350K+ flips. Granite also acceptable. Laminate hurts perceived value significantly in that price range.','Unsupported spans, undermount sink weight','10','Laminate countertops in $350K+ market, damaged/dated tile counters','Quartz countertops are table stakes. Never skip on $350K+ flip.'),
('Bathrooms','Shower Glass Door/Enclosure','replacement','per_home',800,1600,3500,'Frameless glass preferred. Shower curtain is a buyer negative. Sliding glass doors acceptable budget option.','Level and square shower required','10','Shower curtain only, plastic shower doors, damaged enclosure','Frameless shower glass is a high-impact, moderate-cost upgrade buyers notice.'),
('Bathrooms','Tile Shower Regrout/Recaulk','repair','per_home',400,900,2000,'Regrout deteriorated tile joints. Recaulk all corners and transitions. Can dramatically extend life of existing tile.','Substrate damage behind tile','15','Black/missing grout, mold in grout lines, failed caulk at tub/wall joint','Often overlooked. $800 regrout can eliminate need for full bath gut.'),
('Flooring','Tile Removal and Prep','repair','per_home',1000,2500,5000,'Remove existing tile to bare concrete, prep for new flooring. More expensive than install over but often necessary for quality result.','Damaged slab revealed after removal','20','Cracked tile throughout, height transition issues, loose tile','Budget tile removal separately when planning LVP over old tile. Height and adhesive residue matter.'),
('Landscaping','Sod Installation','full','sqft',0.65,0.95,1.50,'St. Augustine sod is standard for Florida flips. Install over prepared soil. Must include irrigation or immediate watering. Bahia is cheaper but lower quality appearance.','Irrigation system adequacy','10','Dead lawn, dirt patches, weeds throughout','Budget St. Augustine sod for any flip where yard is dead. $2,500-6,000 typical for average lot.'),
('Landscaping','Irrigation System Repair','repair','per_home',500,1500,4000,'Broken heads, controller replacement, zone repair. Full install if no irrigation: $3,000-6,000. Many FL homes require irrigation to maintain landscaping.','Underground line damage, pump issues','20','No irrigation system on larger lot, broken heads visible, dry zones','In FL heat, landscaping dies without irrigation. Budget irrigation repair if any scope changes required.'),
('Landscaping','Tree Removal','repair','per_home',500,2000,8000,'Small tree $300-600. Medium $800-1,500. Large $1,500-4,000. Emergency removal (after storm) much higher. Stump grinding: $100-300 per stump.','Root damage to utilities','10','Dead trees, trees touching house/roof, large overhanging branches','FL homeowners insurance may require tree removal near structure. Always inspect.'),
('Miscellaneous','Interior Door Replacement','replacement','per_home',1500,3000,6000,'Hollow core doors throughout. 6-panel colonial is standard. Replace all interior doors on full gut. Install 2-inch door casings. Prehung doors including hardware: $250-400 each.','Non-standard opening sizes','10','Hollow core doors damaged, mismatched doors throughout','Budget $3,000 interior doors and hardware on full gut. High visual impact.'),
('Miscellaneous','Bathroom Mirrors and Accessories','replacement','per_home',400,800,1500,'Frameless mirrors or framed mirrors to match vanity. Towel bars, toilet paper holder, robe hooks per bath. Chrome or brushed nickel to match fixtures.','None significant','5','Missing or dated accessories, builder-grade plastic accessories','$600 in bath accessories and mirrors completes the bathroom without much spend.'),
('Miscellaneous','Mailbox and House Numbers','repair','per_home',100,250,600,'New mailbox ($60-150), house numbers visible from street ($20-80), address stone if neighborhood standard.','HOA requirements on mailbox style','5','No mailbox, damaged mailbox, house numbers not visible','$200 for new mailbox and house numbers. Inspectors and appraisers note address visibility.'),
('Miscellaneous','Radon Mitigation','repair','per_home',800,1200,2500,'Less common in FL than northern states but exists in some areas, especially inland. If testing reveals elevated levels, mitigation system required. Usually 1-day install.','Slab penetration in finished spaces','5','Elevated radon test results (>4 pCi/L)','Test if buyer requests or if property is inland elevated terrain. Budget $1,200 if mitigation needed.');


